# Harness output: 
ode tools/check-*.mjs <url> [shot.png] writes its
# screenshots to the working directory by default. They are evidence of a run,
# not source, and a stale screenshot in a diff is worse than no screenshot.
editor.png
editor-full.png
editor-full-light.png
# ---- Compiled binaries ----
#
# services/transcoding-service/ me teen built artifacts TRACKED the:
#   cmd.exe                  11.9 MB
#   transcoding-service      14.6 MB
#   transcoding-service.exe  14.6 MB
#
# 41 MB of machine-specific output in version control, in a service whose
# Dockerfile builds its own binary inside the image. A Windows .exe living in a
# Linux service directory is the clearest sign these were built by accident on a
# Windows shell rather than produced by the build.
#
# Two costs, both real:
#   - every clone pays 41 MB for nothing, and every future commit re-diffs them
#   - a stale binary in the tree can be run INSTEAD of the built one, which is a
#     genuinely nasty class of bug: the code you edited is not the code you ran
#
# The files stay on disk - this only stops them being tracked. They are build
# output, not source, and docker compose build produces the real binary.
*.exe
services/transcoding-service/transcoding-service